<p>Ukraine is marking the 40th anniversary of the 1986 Chernobyl disaster while warning that Russia&#x27;s war has revived fears of another nuclear emergency near the site. The anniversary has renewed attention on the world&#x27;s worst nuclear accident, which began when reactor No. 4 exploded during a safety test at the plant near Pripyat on April 26, 1986, forcing the permanent evacuation of nearby communities. The remembrance is both historical and immediate. Ukrainian officials say Russian missiles and drones have repeatedly flown near the plant during the war, underscoring how vulnerable nuclear infrastructure remains in armed conflict. Across the coverage, survivors, former cleanup workers and returning visitors describe a site shaped by loss, memory and duty, while anniversary reports revisit the role of liquidators and the consequences of official secrecy in the disaster&#x27;s aftermath.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ykvZ0P1tD_JsTOFvjNUpsGZ5lHqAZmpERitMJxGrw_sgiF3BW2mub2zBr5B7C2PF8Ye4LbuCdOIE8npAlvyHwF69ySam-NzF-Xc5X4XUJGO9mR3WZa778ywe6M7RIh1rn-0csYYuFI77yLIzZyOLEMoWoWq_Oj-RUQXqnKxN7aT94hnWjvRUZJWu0DwlIDQcKLEdU3szgUxjMM0DDld-PVrwxpzHpTRu0Hh3Sy74E2JIPY18tqZ57sS1LdGyANtxW7fbcfY9CBDuPjRIYQ' alt='Workers who helped clean up contamination from the Chernobyl nuclear power plant disaster hold flowers before placing them on a monument to their fallen comrades near the plant in Chernobyl, Ukraine, Tuesday, April 21, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Evacuated city: Pripyat, once home to about 50,000 people, was fully evacuated after the accident and remains one of the clearest symbols of the disaster&#x27;s human dislocation.</li><li>Early secrecy: Soviet authorities first issued only terse statements and struggled to explain the scale of the accident in the weeks that followed.</li><li>Burial legacy: Some of the earliest victims were buried in Moscow after acute radiation sickness struck firefighters and plant workers exposed during the initial response.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Ukrainian authorities: Kyiv says Russia has repeatedly sent missiles and drones along flight paths near the Chernobyl plant, framing the anniversary as a reminder that war can again put nuclear facilities at risk. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/ukraine-marks-40th-anniversary-of-chernobyl-disaster-under-cloud-of-war'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Former residents of Pripyat: A former resident who returned with DW described the city as a place people left forever, underscoring the personal rupture behind the abandoned buildings and overgrown streets. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/40-years-after-chernobyl-pripyat-today/a-76925905'>DW</a>)</li><li>Liquidators: Cleanup workers returning for commemorations told The Globe and Mail that they still see their role in terms of duty and sacrifice, even as they carry lasting physical and emotional consequences from the disaster. (<a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/business/technology/science/article-the-invisible-enemy-40-years-on-from-nuclear-disaster-chornobyl/'>The Globe and Mail</a>)</li><li>Historical reporting: AP&#x27;s retrospective on its original coverage highlights how little reliable information Soviet officials released at first, showing how official secrecy shaped global understanding of the accident. (<a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/ap-early-chernobyl-victims-buried-moscow-cemetery-132387652'>ABC News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/ukraine-marks-40th-anniversary-of-chernobyl-disaster-under-cloud-of-war'>Ukraine marks 40th anniversary of Chernobyl disaster under cloud of war</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/26/world/europe/40-years-ago-a-nuclear-catastrophe-at-chernobyl.html'>40 Years Ago, a Nuclear Catastrophe at Chernobyl</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/ap-early-chernobyl-victims-buried-moscow-cemetery-132387652'>AP Was There: Early Chernobyl victims buried in Moscow cemetery</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://theweek.com/history/the-chernobyl-nuclear-disaster'>The Chernobyl nuclear disaster, 40 years on</a> - theweek.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/40-years-after-chernobyl-pripyat-today/a-76925905'>40 years after Chernobyl: Pripyat today</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/business/technology/science/article-the-invisible-enemy-40-years-on-from-nuclear-disaster-chornobyl/'>The invisible enemy: 40 years on from nuclear disaster, Chornobyl liquidators return</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li></ul>